{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Do not lift a horn</b> — because he is like you, and they are human beings like you." "<b>El</b> — the meaning: it is not enough for you that you lift your horn against your fellows, until your heart is proud to lift it against those exalted above you — and now you speak with a stiff neck — like \"he runs to Him with a neck.\"" "<b>And athaq</b> — an adjective, like \"an atfaq came out of your mouth,\" or it is the adjective of \"neck.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 75, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra parses עתק as a תואר (adjective/descriptive term) modifying צואר (neck); the internal Hebrew quotation in [1] cites ירוץ אליו בצואר from Hosea, and here יצא עתק מפיכם from Proverbs 8:7. Both instances of תואר rendered 'adjective' per his usage."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:37.778733056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}